{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack","id":21063,"title":"\"Supenatural\" Shard ( Empyrean & Inferno Setting Hack )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T01:57:01-08:00","id":21063,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> \"Supenatural\" Shard ( Empyrean & Inferno Setting Hack )","content":"Hi, forum! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Half year ago I proposed some little tweaks for DtD setting to better place it within both World of Darkness cosmology, and be more like the &quot;Supernatural&quot; TV series. Main thought was that Now with my Prestige Edition Rulbook in print and beta corebook on my hard drive, I want to revisit this idea. Here are main points we come to when discussed it previously:<br /> <br /> 1. Both Empyrean &amp; Inferno exists in this version of WoD universe (see <b>Inferno</b> or <b>Promeathean</b> books on this ).<br /> <br /> 2. Angels Covers aren't new beings, they are mortals that Infrastrucutre found most matching the angel's mission and usade his body for it. Basiclly, Angles with they Covers are Possesed ( see <b>Inferno</b> on this subject ). If Unchained loses his Cover, he leaves his host body. There were idea that future Cover need to be Stigamtic or Souless first, but I would put it as Storyteller option.<br /> <br /> 3. Unchained that loses his whole Cover goes to Inferno ( i.e. classical Hell ) and loses one dot of Premium. His ring can call him out of it, but is hard, and they need use Infrastractur or Soul Pact to find new host ( i.e. Cover ) for him.<br /> <br /> 4. Unchained that lose his last dot of Premium by losing Cover goes to Inferno last time and becomes Vice Demon permanentlly. They are called Fallen in constrast to Unchained.<br /> <br /> There where also idea that each journey to Inferno is making Unchained more and more bounded to his Vice. And that there should be why for Empyrean to steal some Unchained for it's cause. Also good name for Empyrean-bound Unchained would be great help in this.<br /> <br /> Hopes you like basic premise and join our little project. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-01-2013, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T02:18:37-08:00","id":30341,"title":"","content":"I really do like &quot;Supernatural&quot;, and already incorporate their treatment of some other things that go bump in the night in my games, so good on ya.<br /> <br /> Caveat to below: I haven't read Inferno or Promethean, they haven't come up in my games yet.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure about having Inferno be the &quot;Penalty Box&quot; for Unchained who go loud or get their Cover whittled down to nothing. Instead, I'd say that Inferno is the realm of an Unchained Agency that 'made it', that have fulfilled their collective vision of Hell in a separate realm devoid of the God Machine that most Tempters envision.<br /> <br /> Going further with this, the Agency has its minions function as the Vice Demons you mention, until the minions gather enough power/pacts/moxie to have minions of their own. Or, so fearful of not being able to return to their castle (or unable to return if they leave?), they use Exploits hitherto unknown to Unchained still in the Fallen Realm to create these little extensions of their intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:00:25-08:00","id":41685,"title":"","content":"I can't say I'm uninterested, but it would be nice to have the archive link here instead of the WW one.<br /> <br /> Just saying..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:08:40-08:00","id":41861,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\">FallenEco</a>, but all important from old topic is in first post. Maybe you could comment on this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:32:18-08:00","id":42125,"title":"","content":"This Inferno is too undefined. Pardon's comment is valid, but seeing as how the way Inferno is described in it's own book and the premise put forward in you're post, it shouldn't be.<br /> The Inferno should not be a place the Unchained want to go too, because that undermines the point of playing the game. Plus it contradicts the 'source material'.<br /> Even demon's shouldn't want to go too that Hell.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the idea that the Inferno was created by the G-M to control the Unchained works well. The Fallen become the G-M attempt at damage control; too altered by their stay to be re-integrated/recycled, they are forced to play in their little corner with little toys rather than the far more disruptive tool set of the Unchained. In exchange, the Fallen are left alone, or at least considered a lower priority.<br /> <br /> As for 'Empyrean-bound Unchained', I need you to be more specific. Are we talking about 'Angels-in-Human suits', 'Angelic Possessed ala Inferno' or &quot;Unchained' Angels'?<br /> As you can see, there is a lot of potential ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T01:29:08-08:00","id":73092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack?p=42125#post42125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the idea that the Inferno was created by the G-M to control the Unchained works well. The Fallen become the G-M attempt at damage control; too altered by their stay to be re-integrated/recycled, they are forced to play in their little corner with little toys rather than the far more disruptive tool set of the Unchained. In exchange, the Fallen are left alone, or at least considered a lower priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more I think about it, the more I see they really should be Agendas, but more ancients cutls than modern intelligance agancy's. They would work for 7 great Demon Princes, and seeing the Vice as thing really distinctive from G-M purpose put on them. They are working for guys higher tham them, but I working for most human things in existance - Vices - not so occult matices of alien God Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack?p=42125#post42125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for 'Empyrean-bound Unchained', I need you to be more specific. Are we talking about 'Angels-in-Human suits', 'Angelic Possessed ala Inferno' or &quot;Unchained' Angels'?<br /> As you can see, there is a lot of potential ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Empyrean Unchained' would be 'Angels-in-Human suits', Virtue equivalent to Fallen. They are allied with other Emprean-bound beings - 'Angelic Possesed ala Inferno' from diffrent spiritual types. I think about calling them Exalted, in oposition to Fallen of Vice side.<br /> <br /> The problem we have now is what would be with demons loosing his Vessel that Infrastucutre give him in the first place? Were goes demons without Covers?<br /> <br /> I will try to write new Agendas in couple of days. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T00:55:11-08:00","id":75474,"title":"","content":"Here is first draft of Inferno's Agenda. Hopes you like it, and point me to the things you don't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Fallen</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Better to reign in Hell, then serve in Heavan</i></span></div> <br /> Demons are sinners. They sinned against God-Machine as angels, and were cast away in return. They sin to potect they Covers, or sin against them. And they sin like any other human, even if they aren\u2019t ones. Truly, to be a demon, is to be slave to the sin. Fallen are it\u2019s masters.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness, sin is power. People feel better if they do \u201cbad things\u201d in name of they Vice. Monsters of the night rave in they darker side, gaining strength in return. Fallen are demons that after rebelion against God-Machine were confronted with existence as creature of Vice. After the Fall, they could empower by serving it. Also, sinning is so sweet.<br /> <br /> And then they find there is literal Hell. Not metaphorical dimension of freedom most demons looking for. But real, Old Testament type Hell. Many call it Inferno. But to Fallen it\u2019s called home.Or at least they want to. For now, it\u2019s place were they Demon Prince patrons live.<br /> <br /> Those ancient beings, old as humanity itself, are very interested in once angels, now demons.They send they lesser servants, spirits, ghosts and other things transformed by the sins they serve. And those massangers are preaching to Unchained so they coud join in Inferno. Some of them do. And so Fall lead to the Fallen.<br /> <br /> But of course they don't forget about God-Machine. As false tyrant that once rules they lives, it should be stopped. Or at least every beautiful Angel he makes been brought to Inferno's Hosts. And Fallen will make them Fall.<br /> <br /> <b>The Descent:</b> Most Unchained wants freedom. They look for Hell in what there aren\u2019t any masters and slaves, only themselves. But without other beings, there isn\u2019t any sociaty, there isn\u2019t hierarchy. <i>Hell is empty and all the devils are here</i> - like they say. But Fallen don\u2019t want to be alone. As once angels, they crave for belonging, orders, purpose. But they can\u2019t return to the God-Machine. They found human side in themselves, individuality, identity.They don\u2019t want to loose those precious gifts of Fall. And so they decide they will reign in literall Hell instead.<br /> <br /> Fallen are both masters and slaves. They work for one of the great Patrons, doing \u201chis work\u201d. But always dreaming on the day when they walk in to Inferno, and took the throne for them. They will finally be those that send commands, not obeying them.<br /> <br /> But for now, they join with rest of Unchained. They forging Vice in to powerful tool of they both inner strength and influence on others, They preach to demons about they own free will, and that they should rule. They tempt Angels in to Fall. And of course, they hide outside of eyes of God-Machine, as it hunts the like the rest of the kind. But at least they have purpose in they life. Someday, when they will be powerful enough, they will Descent in to Inferno and be it\u2019s masters. Now will they gather of the sins of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Fallen join in loose cults dedicated to one of Patrons. They idealise Seven Deadly Sins, working to sustain it in the world, and by it, empowering themselves for they Descent. From time to time they make loose alliances between cults, especially, as they local mission dictates help from in name of many sins.<br /> <br /> Demon Prince Patrons of Fallen in Inferno:<ul><li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucifer\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a>: pride</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammon\" target=\"_blank\">Mammon</a>: greed</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmodai\" target=\"_blank\">Asmodeus</a>: lust</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leviathan\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan</a>: envy</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beelzebub\" target=\"_blank\">Beelzebub</a>: gluttony</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satan\" target=\"_blank\">Satan</a>: wrath</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belphegor\" target=\"_blank\">Belphegor</a>: sloth</li> </ul>But outside they misions, they are totally free. Most join rest of Unchained in they rings, becoming priest- or advisor-like figures, encouraging individuality and free reign of demons. Of course, they play and scheme they on they're comrades, but helping them in the way none the less.<br /> <br /> Many Fallen are ones Integrators, now converted when they see that beside God-Machine they will be only soulless drones at best, destroyed at worst. Confronted with existence of Inferno, they choose they own side. Now have order and missions they lingered, but also work on they own terms. They will join hierarchy, once more, only it is they who would be in charge of it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sterotypes</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Inqusitors:</b> Your knowledge don\u2019t lead you to power, if you don\u2019t take actions.<br /> <b>Integrators:</b> Our misguided brothers and sisters, it\u2019s pity you still don\u2019t see your are just slaves.<br /> <b>Saboteures:</b> Still playing this silly wargame with God-Machine? Your choice, but I\u2019m focused on more grander undertacking right now.<br /> <b>Tempters:</b> Hedonism is good, but you still need commitment to achieve something.<br /> <b>Vampires:</b><br /> <b>Werewolves:</b> One needless rage is a tool in others great plan.<br /> <b>Mages:</b> You command the \u201cdemons\u201d, yet you can\u2019t master your own sins.<br /> <b>Changlings:</b><br /> <b>Human:</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2014, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:18:31-08:00","id":330852,"title":"","content":"What did the link in the OP say for the old forums post? Cant connect anymore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:08:07-08:00","id":330944,"title":"","content":"It was original, first draft of idea, with using Inferno as place where Unchained goes when they &quot;die&quot;. Corrected and refined idea is now in topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/213767-more-classical-demons-and-angels-setting-hack\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">More classical Demons and Angels setting hack</span></span></a>. It's basically version 2.0 of this hack and more coherent with <b>DtD</b> rules, still using Supernatural-like background. I will gladly answer any questions there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-05-2014, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T03:20:56-08:00","id":330949,"title":"","content":"I think linking the World of Darkness to &quot;Supernatural&quot; should be done the other way around: how can we use the rules to create THAT world. Most of my ideas revolve around using Possessed for Demons (though amping their ability to use their powers a little more, by giving them more &quot;fuel&quot; and better spending rate the more powerful they are) and the optional rules for Empyreans for Angels a la Castiel. Some powers (teleportation, for example) are the hardest to justify, but since only the most powerful demons (Crowley, Lucifer, Azazel) have it, it's not too bad. Other creatures can probably be created using the Hunter book's Dread Powers system to make them less insane than their &quot;real&quot; versions are in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}